{"name":"Dark Slate Blue","hex":"#214761","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dark","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having an absolute or (more often) relative lack of light.","Extinguished."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A complete or (more often) partial absence of light.","Ignorance."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dark"},{"term":"slate","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flake or piece of certain types of stone that tend to cleave into thin layers.\n A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made.\n\nA piece of other material used as a roofing tile.","A piece of such stone, usually cut into a rectangular shape, used as a tile for flooring, roofing, etc.;  such tiles collectively, or the material from which they are made."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having the bluish-grey colour of slate (noun etymology 1, noun sense 4)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/slate"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"X11 color names","blocks":[{"text":"In computing, on the X Window System, X11 color names are represented in a simple text file, which maps certain strings to RGB color values. It was traditionally shipped with every X11 installation, hence the name, and is usually located in <X11root>/lib/X11/rgb.txt. The web colors list is descended from it but differs for certain color names."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X11_color_names"},{"title":"Slate","blocks":[{"text":"Slate is a fine-grained, foliated, homogeneous, metamorphic rock derived from an original shale-type sedimentary rock composed of clay or volcanic ash through low-grade, regional metamorphism. It is the finest-grained foliated metamorphic rock. Foliation may not correspond to the original sedimentary layering, but instead is in planes perpendicular to the direction of metamorphic compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f4/Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg/330px-Slate_%28Knife_Lake_Formation%2C_metamorphism_at_2.7_Ga%2C_Neoarchean%3B_Rt._135_roadcut%2C_Gilbert%2C_Minnesota%2C_USA%29_3_%2823140002749%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slate"},{"title":"Darkness","blocks":[{"text":"Darkness is the condition resulting from a lack of illumination, or an absence of visible light."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Creation_of_Light.png/330px-Creation_of_Light.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darkness"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Shades_of_red.png/500px-Shades_of_red.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AShades_of_red.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/500px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/1280px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/93/Slate_with_pyrite.JPG/500px-Slate_with_pyrite.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Slate with pyrite","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASlate_with_pyrite.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/500px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/1280px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg/500px-Slate_outcrop_Porto_Covo_August_2026-7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"